{
  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat → 0.6287 acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion actually adds value over a strong single-modality baseline. config_009 (image_only, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool) is the cleanest ablation of config_001—it uses the same image encoder (ViT-L), same aggregation (avgpool), and same profile setting (multiprofile), differing only in the removal of the RNA branch. If image-only accuracy is close to 0.6287, the RNA signal contributes little and I should redirect budget toward image-centric or different-fusion strategies. If it is substantially lower, multimodal fusion is confirmed as the right direction and I can exploit that in subsequent experiments. This single comparison resolves the highest-impact design question early, making the best use of experiment 2 under a 10-experiment budget."
}

